{"command": "lf help open", "code": 0, "stdout": "Open one conversation here, in a sibling tab, or focus its existing view\n\nUsage: lf open [OPTIONS] [URL]\n\nArguments:\n  [URL]  Work address, such as loopflow://loopflow/task/LOO-507\n\nOptions:\n      --host <HOST>         Destination host; auto uses the calling terminal, never a fallback host [default: auto] [possible values: auto, desktop, cmux, herdr, tmux, rex, terminal]\n      --session <SESSION>   Open this exact Session rather than its scope's primary\n      --diff                Show the Task's Changes browser beside its conversation (Desktop)\n      --link                Print a link without opening or preparing anything\n      --format <FORMAT>     [possible values: text, markdown]\n      --json                \n      --server <SERVER>     Rex Unix socket endpoint\n      --here                Attach in this terminal (direct CLI default)\n      --tab                 Attach in a sibling tab (agent default)\n      --focus               Reveal an existing conversation view; create nothing\n      --file <PATH>         Present original files in an attached Desktop Files view\n  -a, --agent <AGENT>       Select this conversation or all agent steps of this Graph (harness[:model])\n      --setting <SETTINGS>  Override a typed preference for this invocation (KEY=YAML); repeatable\n  -v, --verbose             Show context accounting and diagnostic logs\n  -h, --help                Print help\n\nDirect CLI calls attach here; agent calls open a sibling tab. An already-open conversation stays where it is: use --focus to reveal it, or lf resume to move input. Layouts and overviews: lf workspace.\n", "stderr": ""}
